  "security_implications": "data_in_prev_d may hold sensitive AES intermediate data. The DIP_CLEAR case assigns data_in (current input) instead of clearing data, which could leave uncleared secrets in the register. This violates zeroization expectations for clearing-sensitive state and could lead to information leakage if uncleared data is later observed or persists in debug modes.",
